<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1861) <span class="when">Oct 27, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Versioned stills stay stills</b>: a still named like <i>BOU_040_v004.png</i> opens as one picture, even with its earlier versions in the same folder. The version number was being read as a frame number, so the versions played as a short sequence and a shared review could fall out of step.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1858) <span class="when">Oct 27, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Live Only in the Review Manager</b>: a switch under the filter, on by default, lists just the reviews still running. Beside it, how many ended ones are hidden; click that to show them all.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1855) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Much smaller notes reports</b>: each picture in an exported notes PDF is kept at the size it is printed (sharp in print and zoomed in on screen) instead of the whole 4K frame. A 7-page report that was 295 MB is now about 2 MB.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1852) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Zoom 100% is the source&#8217;s own pixels</b>: an HD review copy of a 4K source zooms to the 4K at 1:1 (with Show Source When Zoomed In on); an HD source shows HD pixel for pixel. The zoom readout and the View menu&#8217;s checks count the same way, so an HD copy of a 4K source reads about 50% at fit.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: the Fit to Window check mark</b> now updates the moment the view changes; in 1849 it could be a step behind.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1849) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: Fit to Window and Zoom 100%</b> are separate again. Where a picture&#8217;s fit was close to 100% (a 1920 picture on a 1920 screen), both were checked and 100% snapped back to fit at the next resize. Now the view stays at the zoom you chose, re-fits only when Fit is chosen, and the View menu checks one or the other.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1846) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: opening a colleague&#8217;s session of Kitsu clips</b>: their clips pointed at the other Mac&#8217;s preview cache, and Asobi searched your folders (all of Downloads) for them with the window empty. Kitsu clips now come from your own preview cache, or are fetched from their Kitsu playlist as the session opens. A clip whose version is no longer in the playlist stays offline, with a line saying so.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1843) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases on other Macs are marked</b>: in the Review Manager, a showcase under On Other Macs has the yellow Showcase tag and its finished / viewers count, as your own do. Click it for its viewing.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1840) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Other Macs&#8217; reviews on their own page</b>: in the Review Manager, clicking a review under On Other Macs shows it on the right, with the studio&#8217;s controls (Join, Pause, Only People Invited, End) and its viewing straight away, as your own reviews do.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
